        "city": "Las Vegas",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging matters in the Las Vegas market",
        "market_text": "<p>A huge share of Las Vegas buyers are shopping from somewhere else — California equity movers, retirees, and investors who may write an offer before they ever fly in. For a buyer who will only see the home through its photos, the photos are the showing, and an empty beige-carpet room tells them nothing.</p><p>Vegas inventory skews new and vacant: spec builds, flipped ranches and investor-owned condos rarely have furniture in them. Virtual staging fills entire vacant houses for less than the cost of renting furniture for one room.</p><p>The volume of near-identical inventory is the other problem. In a Summerlin or Henderson development where a dozen listings share the same three floor plans, the photos are the only thing distinguishing one from another — and an empty version of a plan a buyer has already scrolled past four times gives them no reason to stop.</p><p>That makes Las Vegas a digital-first market. Those buyers start online like almost everyone else: 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search, according to the National Association of Realtors. A staged home gives a vacant listing the living space, scale and warmth that make a property stand out before the first showing — or the first offer.</p><p>Vacant homes look smaller and less appealing in online listings. Virtual staging illustrates a possible furniture layout for each room, and because it's drawn to accurate proportions, buyers can judge the space without being misled about its size. With a diverse pool of buyers — relocating families, retirees, investors and second-home owners — the staging style can be matched to whoever the listing is most likely to attract.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Las Vegas home staging, done virtually",
        "local_text": "<p>Designers stage to the local palette — bright desert-modern for Summerlin and Henderson new builds, clean contemporary for high-rise condos on the Strip corridor. Every image is MLS-ready in 24 to 48 hours with disclosure guidance.</p><p>Second-home and short-term-rental listings get staged for how they'll actually be used, which is rarely the same as a primary residence: flexible sleeping space, an obvious place to put a table, and outdoor areas that read as usable most of the year.</p><p>Files are ready for the Las Vegas REALTORS® MLS with disclosure guidance and full usage rights. There's no consultation to schedule and no crew to hire: order, upload and your designer handles the rest. Volume discounts apply automatically — 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+ — so whole-home sets for Summerlin and Henderson new builds stay affordable.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "Summerlin, Henderson, Green Valley, The Lakes, Southern Highlands, Anthem, Centennial Hills, Strip corridor"
      }
    },
